# position_control store snapshot (_datafiles/messages/position_control.yaml)
# Recorded 2026-09-17 from PRE-migration code: the local substitute() in
# internal/hooks/Position_Messaging.go, a {key} loop over the three authored name
# vocabularies {attacker}/{target}, {Controller}/{Controlled} and {Character}.
# Stand-ins: Actorius is the actor side, Acteeus the actee side.
# dimensions: block x key [x subtype] x role, role in {actor,actee,observer}:
# M4b-1 collapsed this store's three authored KEY vocabularies (attacker/target/
# room, controller/controlled and self/room) the way M4a collapsed its three
# token ones. In the gradient and transition rows the SIDE field is a role too;
# the gradient state spelled `controlled` is authored data and keeps its name.
# Empty rows are authored silence.
# gradient_messages and transition_messages have NO Go reader today; those rows
# guard the data, not a render path.

